From 6d4557d19c95539f2c09cb1eb875a0155de760bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ravindra Lakkireddy <85186928+rlakki08@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 03:05:32 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] texture: tests (masking, front-only UVs, side colours,
 flags, orientation, retexture); resize textured like model.glb

- tests/test_texture.py (22): the white-background flood and its cache, a showroom with neighbours
  (the central product of the part's aspect), the frame-filling crop, a keystoned box face, no
  background in the texture; body/trim sampling and the finish words; recolor keeps Grok's paint;
  front-only UVs on a box, a sphere (60 deg, the footprint not the bbox) and an upright tub; the
  three flags; a backwards CAD model detected, turned and photo'd on its true front; the relief
  pass; retexture without calls (and what it keeps); warm --retexture rows and totals.
- front_relief is now the share of the front view off its main plane (a small proud handle counts).
- a plain-background cut-out is reused whatever the aspect (only picking among objects needs it).
- resize: a resized template is textured like model.glb; _box returns (box, info).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
